+	/*
+	 * bzdOS 2026-08-11: make_dev_alias_p(MAKEDEV_CHECKNAME) instead of
+	 * make_dev_alias(), and keep the resulting cdev so drm_dev_alias_free()
+	 * can destroy it.
+	 *
+	 * make_dev_alias() is make_dev_alias_v(MAKEDEV_WAITOK, ...) — without
+	 * MAKEDEV_CHECKNAME, kern_conf.c PANICS on a name that already exists
+	 * instead of returning EEXIST.  Since nothing here used to destroy the
+	 * alias, the second drm_dev_alloc() for a given minor index in one boot
+	 * always hit that panic.  A driver whose probe fails after
+	 * drm_dev_alloc() and is retried is the ordinary case during bring-up,
+	 * and it took the whole machine down:
